IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gst-types`

-- Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 — GOAL 6: PENALTIES AND OFFENCES.
--
--   "What does a late payment or late return cost; and for each offence, what
--    is the penalty measured by the tax, the fine and the imprisonment; may it
--    be compounded, and does it need the Public Prosecutor's consent?"
--
-- Source: ../source/GSTA1993.txt — Part 9 (ss 58-67), ss 44(4), 46(6), 69,
-- 75, 81(4), 83I, 84(2D)-(2E), 86(1).

§ `Goal 6 — penalties and offences`

-- s 60(1): unpaid tax attracts "(a) a penalty equal to 5% of the amount of tax
-- payable"; and "(b) if the amount of tax outstanding is not paid within
-- 60 days after the imposition of the penalty ..., an additional penalty of 2%
-- of the tax outstanding ... for each completed month that the tax remains
-- unpaid commencing from the date on which the tax became payable, but the
-- total additional penalty must not exceed 50%". FORK F3: the additional
-- penalty runs only once the 60 days have passed, and then counts every
-- completed month from the due date.
@ref s 60(1)
GIVEN tax IS A NUMBER, `days unpaid after the 5% penalty` IS A NUMBER, `completed months unpaid since due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late payment penalty on` tax `, days after the 5% penalty` `days unpaid after the 5% penalty` `, completed months since due` `completed months unpaid since due` MEANS
    tax TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 100 PLUS `the additional penalty`
    WHERE
        `the additional penalty` MEANS
            IF `days unpaid after the 5% penalty` LESS THAN 60 THEN 0
            ELSE IF `completed months unpaid since due` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN 50
                 THEN tax TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100
                 ELSE tax TIMES `completed months unpaid since due` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 60(2): a late return costs "(a) $200; (b) $200 for each completed month
-- that the taxable person continues not to make the return ...", "not
-- exceeding in any case $10,000".
@ref s 60(2)
GIVEN `completed months late` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late return penalty, completed months late` `completed months late` MEANS
    IF `uncapped` GREATER THAN 10000 THEN 10000 ELSE `uncapped`
    WHERE
        `uncapped` MEANS 200 PLUS 200 TIMES `completed months late`

-- s 61(c)-(e): failing to register costs "a penalty equal to 10% of the tax
-- due in respect of each year or part thereof", a fine up to $10,000, and "$50
-- for every day ... after conviction".
@ref s 61(c)
GIVEN `tax due` IS A NUMBER, `years or part years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the failure-to-register penalty on` `tax due` `, years or parts` `years or part years` MEANS
    `tax due` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `years or part years`

-- The maximum for each offence. s 58: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and in
-- default of payment to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months" (the
-- 6 months is imprisonment in default, recorded here as the term). ss 59, 62,
-- 62B, 63, 64, 64A: a penalty measured in multiples of the tax.
@ref ss 44(4), 46(6), 58, 59, 61, 62, 62A, 62B, 62C, 63, 64, 64A, 65, 66, 81(4), 83I(4), (9), 84(2D)-(2E), 86(1)
GIVEN o IS A `GST offence`
GIVETH A `GST penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 44(4) receipts`                                                   THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 5000,   0,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 46(6) records, first conviction`                                  THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 5000,   6,   TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 46(6) records, second or later conviction`                        THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  36,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 58 an offence with no penalty provided`                           THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 5000,   6,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 59(1) an incorrect return`                                        THEN `GST penalty` OF 1, 0,      0,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 59(2) an incorrect return without reasonable excuse or through negligence` THEN `GST penalty` OF 2, 5000, 36, TRUE, 0
    WHEN `s 61 failing to register or notify`                                 THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  0,   FALSE, 50
    WHEN `s 62 wilful evasion`                                                THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 10000,  84,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 62A misrepresenting status to an overseas supplier`               THEN `GST penalty` OF 1, 10000,  0,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 62B wilfully misrepresenting status`                              THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 10000,  84,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 62C(1) participating in a fraudulent arrangement`                 THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 500000, 120, TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 62C(4) a business used for a fraudulent arrangement`              THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 50000,  12,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 63 improperly obtaining a refund`                                 THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 10000,  36,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 64 dealing in goods or services where tax is evaded`              THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 5000,   0,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 64A(1) collecting tax without authority`                          THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 10000,  0,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 64A(2) collecting tax without authority, negligently`             THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 10000,  36,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 64A(4) a registered person over-collecting, negligently`          THEN `GST penalty` OF 3, 10000,  36,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 65 an officer's or impersonator's misconduct`                     THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  36,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 66 obstructing the Comptroller`                                   THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  12,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 81(4) failing to give security`                                   THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 5000,   0,   FALSE, 0
    WHEN `s 83I(4) refusing to answer on examination`                         THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  12,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 83I(9) false information on examination`                          THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  24,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 84(2D) not complying with a notice`                               THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  12,  TRUE,  100
    WHEN `s 84(2E) false information to the Comptroller`                      THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  24,  TRUE,  0
    WHEN `s 86(1) contravening orders or regulations`                         THEN `GST penalty` OF 0, 10000,  24,  TRUE,  0

-- s 62(2): a false statement or entry in a return "is presumed, until the
-- contrary is proved, to have [been] made ... with intent to evade tax". s
-- 62C(6): a defence to (4) if used "without the person's knowledge" and the
-- person "took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence". s 59(3):
-- s 59 does not apply to a claim on a tainted chain.
@ref s 62C(4)-(6)
GIVEN `used for the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN, `without knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director, partner or proprietor is guilty under s 62C(4), used:` `used for the arrangement` `, without knowledge:` `without knowledge` `, due diligence:` `reasonable precautions and due diligence` IF
    `used for the arrangement` AND NOT (`without knowledge` AND `reasonable precautions and due diligence`)

-- s 74(1): an officer of a body that commits an offence is deemed guilty
-- unless the offence was "without the person's consent or connivance" and the
-- person "exercised all such diligence".
@ref s 74(1)
GIVEN `without consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed guilty, without consent:` `without consent or connivance` `, diligence:` `exercised all due diligence` IF
    NOT (`without consent or connivance` AND `exercised all due diligence`)

-- s 75(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not
-- exceeding $5,000".
@ref s 75(1)
GIVEN prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` prescribed MEANS
    IF prescribed THEN JUST 5000 ELSE NOTHING

-- s 69: no prosecution under "section 6, 62, 62C, 63, 65 or 66 except with the
-- consent of the Public Prosecutor".
@ref s 69
GIVEN o IS A `GST offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor's consent is needed for` o IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 62 wilful evasion`                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 62C(1) participating in a fraudulent arrangement`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 62C(4) a business used for a fraudulent arrangement`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 63 improperly obtaining a refund`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 65 an officer's or impersonator's misconduct`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 66 obstructing the Comptroller`                       THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 73A(1): a notice to attend court in place of a summons for an offence
-- "punishable by a fine or by an imprisonment term not exceeding 12 months or
-- both".
@ref s 73A(1)
GIVEN o IS A `GST offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice to attend court may be used for` o IF
        ((`the maximum penalty for` o)'s `fine` GREATER THAN 0 OR (`the maximum penalty for` o)'s `imprisonment in months` GREATER THAN 0)
    AND (`the maximum penalty for` o)'s `imprisonment in months` AT MOST 12

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 6(2), (6B), (6BB), (6CC), (9B), 21(8)-(9), 33(2D), 62(3)-(5), 62B(2), 64A(3), (5), 67, 70-72, 76, 77, 82(5), 89
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`penalty provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 6: secrecy offences (penalty under s 58)"
         "s 21(8)-(9): tax on zero-rated goods found in Singapore becomes payable, and may be waived"
         "s 62(3)-(5): computer manipulation is fraud; evading tax includes obtaining refunds and credits"
         "s 62B(2): a device's location is information given"
         "s 64A(3), (5): who may lawfully collect tax"
         "s 67: tax remains payable; penalties are not tax"
         "ss 70-72, 76, 77: other proceedings, evidence and jurisdiction"
         "s 82(5): leaving Singapore under a travel ban (penalty under s 58)"
         "s 89: remission of tax and penalties"
